A simple test firmware. This code is in the public domain. Simply copy whatever
you can use.

Two images are built from this directory:

- `firmware.hex` — full suite (`start.S` + `hello.c` + sieve/mul/stats + `tests/*.S`).
  Used by `make test` / `make test_verilator`.
- `hello.hex` — `start.S` compiled with `-DHELLO_ONLY` plus `hello.c` / `print.c` /
  `irq.c`. Prints `hello world`, writes the pass magic at `0x20000000`, then
  `ebreak`. Used by `make test_hello` / `make test_verilator_hello`.

Both `.hex` files are **committed prebuilts** (Linux `riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc` +
`make firmware/hello.hex firmware/firmware.hex`) so Windows MSVC cmake-system
can run with `PICO_REBUILD_FIRMWARE=OFF` and no RISC-V GCC. Rebuild on Linux
with the Makefile when firmware sources change.

`print.c` writes bytes to `0x10000000` (testbench UART). The pass store is
`0x20000000 <- 123456789` (see `start.S` and `testbench.v`).
